<title>UK: BOE's George says EMU conditions &quot;unpromising&quot;.</title>
<headline>BOE's George says EMU conditions &quot;unpromising&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said the economic conditions for European monetary union remained &quot;somewhat unpromising.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;There has been an increasing realisation of the political commitment to monetary union on the continent, especially on the part of Chancellor Kohl and President Chirac, even though the economic conditions for monetary union remain somewhat unpromising,&quot; he told a news conference.  </p>
<p>George was speaking at a news conference at which senior Bank officials presented a report entitled &quot;Practical Issues Arising from the Introduction of the Euro.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
